 ## Meaning
 
-甲乙 is a noun for the first and the second, like A and B. In a contract, 甲 labels the first party and 乙 the second, so 甲乙 can name both parties together. The word also means relative merit: which of two things is better. JMdict lists the set phrase 甲乙つけがたい (こうおつつけがたい) as its own entry: "difficult to say which of the two is better."
